BT /F1 10 Tf 50 720 Td (IN THE MADRAS HIGH COURT \(MADURAI BENCH\)
AT MADURAI

CASE NO: W.P.\(MD\) No. 6712 of 2026
CNR NUMBER: HCMD010678902026
DECISION DATE: 2026-02-05
YEAR: 2026

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Justice G.R. Swaminathan

PARTIES:
T. Packiaraj \(Temple Worshipper\)
... Appellant\(s\) / Petitioner\(s\)
Versus
The Commissioner, HR&CE Department, Chennai & Joint Commissioner, Madurai
... Respondent\(s\) / State

STATUTORY PROVISIONS & ACTS REFERRED:
Tamil Nadu Hindu Religious and Charitable Endowments Act 1959, Constitution of India

SECTIONS & CLAUSES UNDER CONSIDERATION:
HR&CE Act Section 78, HR&CE Act Section 79, Article 226

KEY LEGAL DOMAINS & TOPICS:
Temple Lands, HR&CE, Encroachment, Public Trust, Parens Patriae

================================================================================
                                   JUDGMENT
================================================================================

1. FACTUAL MATRIX:
Encroachers erected commercial shops on 12 acres of ancient temple property in Madurai without valid lease. HR&CE failed to enforce eviction under Section 78.

2. ISSUES FRAMED FOR ADJUDICATION:
1. Does the Court have duty under Parens Patriae jurisdiction to protect temple properties from unlawful alienation?

3. STATUTORY FRAMEWORK & PRECEDENTS:
Sections 78 and 79 HR&CE Act grant summary powers to evict encroachers of religious endowments.

4. RATIO DECIDENDI:
Idol is a perpetual minor; High Court exercising Parens Patriae jurisdiction is duty-bound to order eviction of encroachers from temple lands.

5. FINAL DISPOSITION & ORDER:
Writ Petition Allowed; HR&CE Department directed to recover encroached temple lands within 90 days.

Decreed and ordered accordingly.

Hon'ble Justice G.R. Swaminathan
Madras High Court \(Madurai Bench\)
[LEXGUARD CRYPTOGRAPHIC VERIFIED REPOSITORY RECORD]
